    "what_this_means": "They trailed 2-0 into the third inning. Rice's first blast came in that moment. The kind of swing that shifts a game from deficit to control. By the time the inning ended, six runs had crossed and the lead was insurmountable. The bullpen did not need to be heroic; Chivilli threw two scoreless innings in the middle frames, then Hill closed it out without drama. This was not a rescue operation. It was a team that showed up and stayed ahead. That is the cleaner version of a win. Early power translating directly into margin, no escape required late. The problem, of course, is consistency. They just came off seven losses in ten games. One 12-run night does not erase that. Good teams do not let one strong game become a false bottom. But for today, at least, they remembered how to swing through the middle of the order.",
    "what_to_watch": "Carson Palmquist takes the mound for Washington tonight with a 7.11 ERA. Ryan Weathers gets the ball for the Yankees. If the bats show up the way they did in Tampa, this is a winnable matchup.",
